==Enemy==
Sunfish Jones moves slowly, does moderate damage with a relatively long attack interval, but has a lot of health, extreme range with no blind spot, and a 30% chance to slow your cats down for 3 seconds.

==Strategy==
Since Sunfish Jones has massive range, the only realistic way to deal with him is to create an opening by defeating the enemies' frontline first. Once exposed, no amount of stealth can protect him from the likes of [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale Cat]] and [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]]. An alternative is to use [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]]/[[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attackers]], but that is rarely an option, as Long Distance units usually do not pierce that far and waves may fail to consistently hit him.

An excellent unit to use against Sunfish Jones is [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]], due to his attack, HP, and [[Resistant|Resistance]] vs. Angels as well as having only one knockback. Cats like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare]] nukers/rushers make quick work of Jones, as their massive DPS can turn him into fish meat. Just make sure to clear out any peons with the [[Cat Cannon]] or support units. His somewhat low damage for his extreme range allows them to tank a few hits from him, making the window for them to be sent out much bigger, as well as allowing them to land more hits on him.

